Switch 2 (Kodi port) Pillow patch 0003: PIL.features.pilinfo() with a built-in Image.core.

In the Switch 2 port PIL._imaging is a built-in module (inittab, CPython patch 0013), which has no
__file__; pilinfo() printed os.path.dirname(Image.core.__file__) and so raised AttributeError. It now
prints "built-in" for that line. (Patch 0002, for the dropped _webp module, no longer exists.)
--- a/src/PIL/features.py
+++ b/src/PIL/features.py
@@ -243,7 +243,9 @@
         file=out,
     )
     print(
-        f"Binary modules loaded from {os.path.dirname(Image.core.__file__)}",
+        # Switch 2 (Kodi port): Image.core is a built-in module there, without __file__.
+        f"Binary modules loaded from "
+        f"{os.path.dirname(getattr(Image.core, '__file__', None) or 'built-in/')}",
         file=out,
     )
     print("-" * 68, file=out)
